{
  "$schema": "../../schema/livery.schema.json",
  "id": "x-at-kw-ani",
  "airline": "ASA",
  "name": "Xáat Kwáani (\"Salmon People\")",
  "kind": "special",
  "confidence": "medium",
  "drawnOn": "B738",
  "description": "Fuselage: Crystal Kaakeeyáa Worl's formline art nose to tail on white, in Midnight Blue, Atlas Blue and Pink. Two salmon face forward. The first one's head is the front of the aircraft: a navy chin and jaw, an Atlas-blue cap round the cockpit, a pink line (the artist calls it the lifeline) running back from the radome into its mouth, and a big ringed eye behind the forward door. A midnight gill line falls from crown to belly behind the head and a pink-filled dorsal fin sits over the windows ahead of the wing. The second salmon's head is ahead of the fin, its eye by the aft door, with pink cheek forms. Cheatlines: none. Tail: the second salmon's body climbs the fin in white formline on Atlas blue with a column of pink dots, its tail fanned white at the tip. Engines: Atlas-blue cowlings with two rounded midnight forms low down. Winglets: Atlas blue with a small white salmon. Titles: a white 'Alaska' over the wing root on Atlas blue, about half the standard size; 'Xáat Kwáani' in pink and 'SALMON PEOPLE' small on the nose. Artwork: 'Xáat Kwáani' means Salmon People in Tlingit. Colors hex: not published; colors approximate.",
