  "history": "Same airframe previously wore 'Salmon-Thirty-Salmon II' (whole-body king salmon, 2012) which was retired April 2023 and replaced by this design. The original Salmon-Thirty-Salmon (2005) was on 737-400 N792AS.",
  "notes": "Drawn 2026-11-28 on the 737-800 from the left side (Tampa 2023-11-07, Commons file named for a Delta 757; N559AS taxis in the foreground), registered to the drawing by the nose, both doors and the fin tip; checked against the right side (Santa Barbara departure, 2024-07-16) and Alaska's own press photos, which show the same layout mirrored so both salmon face forward on each side. The areas are the big color fields only (docs/LOGOS.md): the navy nose and jaw, the blue cockpit cap, the crown wave, the dorsal fin form, the fields round the title and registration, the navy aft body, the tail salmon's white head and the fin's white body and fanned tail. The eyes, lifeline, gill line, U-forms and pink accents are the logos'. These replace the 2026-11-18 grid-sampled fields, which read as blotches. The wing and engine hide the lower body under the wing root on both sides in every photo; there it's left white over a navy belly. A 2025-03-24 photo shows it still flying in the scheme. The Commons category for N559AS also holds older Salmon-Thirty-Salmon II photos (2018-2019), not used.",
  "from": "2023-05",
